    "status": "active",
    "job": "Pick which of my progress rules fire for my current numbers and give the adjustment each carries",
    "description": "Takes one value per metric (signals) and the person's rules. A rule fires when its metric has a number and the number lies in the rule's half-open band [min, max) (an omitted min is minus infinity, an omitted max is plus infinity). Answers the fired rules with the value that fired them, their adjustments in rule order, and whether any fired. Rules may overlap, so several can fire. Metrics, bands and adjustments are the person's; the tool knows none.",
    "input_schema": {
     "type": "object",
     "required": [
      "signals",
      "rules"
     ],
